Build the size-constrained primary bootstraps with `-Oz`.

The i386 primary bootstraps must fit a fixed number of disk sectors, and
under GCC 15 several no longer do:

    ### bootxx_ext2fs size 8020 is larger than 7680
    ### bootxx_ustarfs size 9196 is larger than 8192

They are already compiled `-Os -ffreestanding -fomit-frame-pointer` with no
stack protector -- I checked the actual compile line rather than assuming,
since injected nixpkgs hardening flags would have been the cheaper
explanation and they are not present. There is no slack to reclaim from
flags that should not have been there; GCC 15 simply emits a few percent
more code than the GCC 12 NetBSD builds this with. For scale, `bootxx_ffsv1`
still fits, but with only 88 bytes to spare.

`-Oz` is what NetBSD itself reaches for here: `bootxx_ustarfs` and
`bootxx_msdos` already carry `OPT_SIZE.clang += -Oz` for exactly this
overflow under clang. GCC grew `-Oz` in GCC 12, so add the matching line
for gcc. `bootxx_msdos` has not been observed to overflow, but upstream has
already identified it as living at the same margin as `ustarfs`, so it gets
the same treatment rather than waiting to trip over it.

--- a/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_ext2fs/Makefile
+++ b/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_ext2fs/Makefile
@@ -3,3 +3,4 @@
 FS=ext2fs
 
 .include <../Makefile.bootxx>
+OPT_SIZE.gcc += -Oz
--- a/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_ustarfs/Makefile
+++ b/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_ustarfs/Makefile
@@ -9,3 +9,4 @@
 
 .include <../Makefile.bootxx>
 OPT_SIZE.clang += -Oz
+OPT_SIZE.gcc += -Oz
--- a/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_msdos/Makefile
+++ b/sys/arch/i386/stand/bootxx/bootxx_msdos/Makefile
@@ -9,3 +9,4 @@
 
 .include <../Makefile.bootxx>
 OPT_SIZE.clang += -Oz
+OPT_SIZE.gcc += -Oz
